{"kind":"finding","id":"F-map-render-006-01","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/MapRender/CrossMemberSeamStitcherTests.cs","line":284,"method":"TangentFromPositions_FirstDifference_IsTheSegmentDirection","category":"T3","severity":"Medium","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/MapRender/CrossMemberSeamStitcher.cs:188; halve the returned difference -> test stays GREEN; it reds only after the tolerance is tightened","what_it_asserts":"That TangentFromPositions((0,0,0),(3,4,0)) returns roughly (3,4).","why_weak":"The third argument 4f binds xUnit 2.4.2's float tolerance overload (not the int precision overload, which a float literal cannot bind), so the accepted window is +/-4.0 around 3 and 4. Any x in [-1,7] and y in [0,8] passes, including a zero, halved or sign-flipped y. This is the only test of the tangent the G1 seam predicate consumes.","proposed_action":"Use a real tolerance, e.g. Assert.Equal(3f, t.x, 1e-4f) and Assert.Equal(4f, t.y, 1e-4f), and add the z component.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
{"kind":"finding","id":"F-map-render-006-02","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/MapRender/CrossMemberSeamStitcherTests.cs","line":317,"method":"Stitch_ComposesAfterRemap_HeadIsReAnchored_NotTheRawSampleUT","category":"T3","severity":"Medium","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/MapRender/CrossMemberSeamStitcher.cs:290; drive DriveUT from the raw liveUT instead of the re-anchored head -> red on the expectedHead assert; the sa.DriveUT==sb.DriveUT assert can never red","what_it_asserts":"That two identical TryStitchDescentSeam calls both return DriveUT == recordedDeorbitUT + (liveUT - triggerUT).","why_weak":"The comment claims the ordering contract is proven by passing a deliberately-wrong sampleUT, but TryStitchDescentSeam has no sampleUT parameter and the two calls use identical arguments, so the independence assertion is a tautology. What remains is the DriveUT value, already asserted by Stitch_TriggeredDescentMember_PromotesVisibleTracedPathDescent, leaving the compose-after-remap ordering contract untested.","proposed_action":"Either exercise the ordering through the caller that supplies the post-remap sample (ChainSampler.Sample) with a perturbed remap, or drop the second call and the sampleUT wording so the test only claims what it proves.","effort":"M","july_ref":"none"}
